WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
The chair now goes to the Amici Qurey who are present here this morning and with the permission

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.000
of our esteemed former chief justices and justice at the Supreme Court, maybe recognize

3
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
them in the order of their seniority in the court.

4
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
So with their permission, former chief justice Artemio Panganiban, maybe recognize you first.

5
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:31.920
You may speak from where you're seated or you can use any of the two rose rooms at your left or at your right at your convenience

6
00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:42.760
Your honor

7
00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.480
Senate president chair win Kachalian

8
00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:49.040
presiding officer Francis

9
00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:51.880
escudero and

10
00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:53.200
esteemed

11
00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.920
senator judges.

12
00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:59.560
May it please the honorable Senate

13
00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:03.640
in performing its constitutional duty and power

14
00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:08.560
to try and decide impeachment cases.

15
00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:14.080
Thank you for inviting this humble retired Chief Justice

16
00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:17.040
as Amicus Curay.

17
00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:19.560
Thank you too for allowing me to speak first,

18
00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:28.320
to attend this afternoon's award ceremony of the Foundation for Liberty and Prosperity,

19
00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:38.640
where 20 exemplary loss callers will be granted 250,000 each, five MBA fellows will be granted

20
00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:45.840
500,000 each, and five dissertation writing contest winners will be conferred more than

21
00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:55.080
1.3 million pesos in prices. In fact, your honors assisting me today are the past recipients

22
00:01:55.080 --> 00:02:07.800
of these FLP awards. Arbim Cortez at my back, Rachel Helya and Jacob Barbosa. Since I will

23
00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:12.800
I will submit a copy of my written brief to you, your honors.

24
00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:16.640
And together with my column on the

25
00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:20.320
in the Philippine Daily Inquirer, August 17,

26
00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:25.320
2026, titled "Two Thirds."

27
00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:31.960
I will confine my remarks today to only four points.

28
00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:32.800
Points.

29
00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:38.020
Point one.

30
00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:43.720
As is generally known, an impeachment trial in the Senate

31
00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:48.720
is sui generis, Latin words that mean of its own kind

32
00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:52.560
or unique.

33
00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:57.560
It has both legal and political connotations.

34
00:02:57.560 --> 00:03:07.400
Parsu wants to its legal character, the honorable senators conduct the trial in accordance with

35
00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:12.220
the law and evidence and the rules of court.

36
00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:19.480
With the Cesar examined by eagle-eyed lawyers ready to overwhelm them.

37
00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:26.400
Our people see senators garbed in their majestic crimson robes.

38
00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:33.720
arguing as if they were in a judicial courtroom. Politically on the other hand,

39
00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:41.720
the composition is not confined to lawyers or jurists. Rather, its membership is

40
00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:48.640
open to elected political leaders who need not obtain formal legal education,

41
00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:58.440
need not pass the excruciating bar examination and need not be scrutinized by the judicial

42
00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:08.840
and bar council. Your owners are not sitting here as justices or lawyers. Truly, the Constitution

43
00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:15.920
does not require you to be lawyers or jurists. Neither are your owners expected to act

44
00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:20.320
like jurists or lawyers.

45
00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:24.680
Notably, senators in the United States of America

46
00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:29.520
trying impeachment cases do not ape judges.

47
00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:33.240
They do not even wear judicial robes.

48
00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:38.040
Instead, they are garbed in their normal attire.

49
00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:43.760
But in this hall, you have deemed it necessary and proper

50
00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:46.720
that you are garbed in judicial robes.

51
00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:52.720
That's why in my case, I want to honor also this honorable court

52
00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:57.040
by being garbed in my judicial robe.

53
00:04:57.040 --> 00:05:00.840
Point two, the Constitution, as has been stated

54
00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:06.080
by the honorable presiding officer, states, and I quote,

55
00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:10.440
"The Senate shall have the sole power to try and decide

56
00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:13.080
all cases of impeachment.

57
00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:17.840
When sitting for that purpose, the senator shall be on oath

58
00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:21.800
or affirmation, which you already have done.

59
00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:25.120
And then, critically, no person shall

60
00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:30.040
be convicted without the concurrence of two-thirds

61
00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:33.800
of all the members of the Senate.

62
00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:36.760
Close quotation.

63
00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:40.520
How do judges and justices interpret

64
00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:42.840
the provisions of the Constitution

65
00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:46.120
and for that matter, of laws.

66
00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:50.360
There are two major ways or methods.

67
00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:57.480
The first method is called verba legis.

68
00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:02.240
Words are plainly read and given their ordinary meanings.

69
00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:05.160
In such cases, there is to quote the Supreme Court

70
00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:09.200
of the Philippines, no need for interpretation,

71
00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:13.160
but only application of the provisions.

72
00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:14.840
Close quotation.

73
00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:19.140
The Senate, as we all know, has 24 members

74
00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:21.140
under the Constitution.

75
00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:26.800
Two-thirds of 24 is mathematically 16.

76
00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:32.000
Therefore, 16 votes are necessary to convict.

77
00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:34.920
If we must use mathematics.

78
00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:43.420
Indeed, mathematics, your honors, is an exact science in the abstract.

79
00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:47.880
To repeat, in the abstract, why?

80
00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:52.280
Because 2 plus 2 is always 4 in the abstract.

81
00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:56.000
3 plus 3 equals 6.

82
00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:59.840
2 times 10 equals always 20.

83
00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:06.280
Therefore, 24 multiplied by 2/3 is always 16 in the abstract.

84
00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:12.320
But not always in reality.

85
00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:17.080
There's a difference between abstraction and reality.

86
00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:19.520
For example, your honors.

87
00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:21.160
Very simple.

88
00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:26.120
One small drop of water, when put together with another

89
00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:36.360
a small drop of water may become one bigger drop of water.

90
00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:41.040
So in reality, it is one big drop of water.

91
00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:49.080
Reality sometimes, your honor, changes the denominator

92
00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:51.240
in mathematics.

93
00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:54.520
In the same way, constitutional interpretation

94
00:07:54.520 --> 00:07:59.160
cannot always stop at abstract mathematics.

95
00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:02.880
We must look at the intent and the purpose

96
00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:06.480
of constitutional provisions, the circumstances

97
00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:12.480
in which they operate and the goals they seek to achieve.

98
00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:17.680
Which brings us to the second method of interpretation,

99
00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:21.840
the Russia-ledges-est anima.

100
00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:24.080
or to quote the Supreme Court,

101
00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:27.600
"The reason of the law is the soul of the law,"

102
00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:29.440
close quotation.

103
00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:32.720
The text must be understood

104
00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:36.000
within its constitutional ambiance.

105
00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:40.240
To shorten my presentation,

106
00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:42.720
as we have time limits,

107
00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:47.000
I will leave it to my more learned retired colleagues

108
00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:48.520
here present,

109
00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:52.800
the jurisprudence on these two ways of interpretation.

110
00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:56.840
However, your honor, I have included in the footnotes

111
00:08:56.840 --> 00:09:00.360
of my presentation the jurisprudence

112
00:09:00.360 --> 00:09:05.320
beginning with the 1924 case of Fuentes

113
00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:07.760
versus Director of Prisons.

114
00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:12.760
And the often quoted 1949 case of Abilino versus Cuenco,

115
00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:18.240
which is only the second, not the first, your honor,

116
00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:19.960
on this issue.

117
00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:22.960
Although in the case of Fuentes, this

118
00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:25.880
was decided prior to the Constitution,

119
00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:29.400
but under the Jones law, which was the enabling

120
00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:35.760
act of the Philippines at the time in 1924.

121
00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:38.520
From the case of a Bellino versus Cuenco,

122
00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:40.400
there are several other cases.

123
00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:46.880
Up to the 2026 case of Henry Leo versus Senate,

124
00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:50.080
with which your honors must be familiar,

125
00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:53.080
since it also involved the present Senate

126
00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:56.200
and the present vice president.

127
00:09:56.200 --> 00:10:01.040
Relevantly, your honors may ask, should the interpretation

128
00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:06.160
of the drafters of the Constitution prevail?

129
00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:10.800
With due respect, not necessarily.

130
00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:15.960
In our constitutional allocation and separation of powers,

131
00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:19.920
the principle of checks and balances,

132
00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:24.960
the makers of the law are not the final authorities

133
00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:27.640
on interpretation.

134
00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:32.880
That delicate task is lodged in an independent branch

135
00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:36.080
of government, the judiciary.

136
00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:42.560
And in the present case, the honorable Senate.

137
00:10:42.560 --> 00:10:47.280
Point three, which of the two modes of interpretation

138
00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:51.120
should the Senate use in discharging its constitutional

139
00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:56.120
duty to try and decide impeachment cases?

140
00:10:57.500 --> 00:11:02.500
I respectfully submit your honors that it is neither.

141
00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:07.120
Repeat, neither of the two.

142
00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:08.200
Why?

143
00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:12.560
Because as I already said, senators are not jurists.

144
00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:14.360
They're not even lawyers.

145
00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:16.600
Some of you may be lawyers, but you're not

146
00:11:16.600 --> 00:11:19.800
called here to decide as lawyers.

147
00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:22.480
You're called upon by the Constitution

148
00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:23.800
to decide as lawmakers.

149
00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:30.240
In fact, your honors, you need not even

150
00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:35.760
use language or methods of magistrates with your respect.

151
00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:40.660
You are elected as representatives at large

152
00:11:40.660 --> 00:11:42.660
of the entire electorate.

153
00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:49.700
You are the co-equals of the justices of the Supreme Court.

154
00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:54.800
So how then should the Constitution be interpreted

155
00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:57.240
by the honorable senators?

156
00:11:57.240 --> 00:12:01.120
In my humble opinion, in accordance with their mandate

157
00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:03.520
as representatives of the people,

158
00:12:03.520 --> 00:12:08.100
especially reflecting the common sense of the people

159
00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:12.000
guided by two fundamental standards,

160
00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:17.000
namely truth and fairness.

161
00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:20.800
Truth and fairness.

162
00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:25.800
The standard of truth is called from facts extracted.

163
00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:30.400
One, from studying and verifying the documents

164
00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:34.340
and papers submitted by the parties.

165
00:12:34.340 --> 00:12:38.120
And two, from hearing witnesses

166
00:12:38.120 --> 00:12:42.780
and observing their demeanor understand in front of you.

167
00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:49.520
The tweets of their eyes, their body language,

168
00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:54.520
the tone of their voices, and the spontaneity of their answers.

169
00:12:55.860 --> 00:12:59.380
By watching and listening to them face to face,

170
00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:06.620
Your Honours would know whether the witnesses are telling the truth, the whole truth, and

171
00:13:06.620 --> 00:13:10.440
nothing but the truth.

172
00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:16.460
Fairness on the other hand demands that we hear before we condemn and that all sides

173
00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:22.340
are given the opportunity to explain their language and actions.

174
00:13:22.340 --> 00:13:31.660
It is what lawyers call due process and what ordinary people believe as fairness.

175
00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:40.980
As the Greek philosopher, Tim Stockless, who was not a lawyer, once said and I quote,

176
00:13:40.980 --> 00:13:47.020
"Strike me as you may, but hear me first."

177
00:13:47.020 --> 00:13:56.240
Truly, I respectfully submit that active participation and independent evaluation of the evidence

178
00:13:56.240 --> 00:14:05.020
are essential to discharge the Senators and the Senators' constitutional responsibility.

179
00:14:05.020 --> 00:14:12.380
Point four, is the judgment of the Senate based on truth and fairness, appealable to

180
00:14:12.380 --> 00:14:15.520
the Supreme Court?

181
00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:18.460
a respectful answer is a big no.

182
00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:23.000
Because there is no constitutional provision

183
00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:25.500
allowing such an appeal.

184
00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:29.580
The Senate's decision is final and unappealable.

185
00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:34.800
The only way, the only way by which the court

186
00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:38.360
can review a Senate decision or order

187
00:14:38.360 --> 00:14:43.360
is when the Senate commits grave abuse of discretion.

188
00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:52.080
Repeat, not just ordinary abuse of discretion, but grave abuse of discretion.

189
00:14:52.080 --> 00:14:58.160
Grave abuse of discretion, your Honours, is not defined by the Constitution.

190
00:14:58.160 --> 00:15:07.560
But jurisprudence characterizes it as, if I may quote, capricious or whimsical or arbitrary

191
00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:13.540
exercise of judgment amounting to lack or excess of jurisdiction.

192
00:15:13.540 --> 00:15:22.600
In simpler terms, the court does not review the Senate's judgment merely because the court

193
00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:29.460
disagrees with the judgment, merely because the court disagrees with the wisdom of the

194
00:15:29.460 --> 00:15:41.260
judgment. No, judicial review arises only when the Senate exercises its power in a capricious,

195
00:15:41.260 --> 00:15:48.820
whimsical, or arbitrary manner, thereby going beyond the limits of its constitutional

196
00:15:48.820 --> 00:15:49.820
authority.

197
00:15:49.820 --> 00:16:05.020
Thus, the Senate must hear the prosecution and the defense witnesses, as it already does,

198
00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:11.020
allow their councils to argue verbally and in writing, and study their presentations

199
00:16:11.020 --> 00:16:12.020
deeply.

200
00:16:12.020 --> 00:16:18.420
Only thereafter should it issue its orders and decisions.

201
00:16:18.420 --> 00:16:25.260
In this connection, is it truthful and fair to allow senators to cast their votes despite

202
00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:29.060
being absent from the proceedings?

203
00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:35.820
Is it fair and truthful should these senators be allowed to vote, though they were there

204
00:16:35.820 --> 00:16:43.980
in hiding, abroad, legally detained, sick, hospitalized, or otherwise absent and have

205
00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:52.300
not been able to access and examine the documents, have not heard the testimonies and have not

206
00:16:52.300 --> 00:17:00.280
observed the demeanor of the witnesses? To put it more picturesly, your honor, is it

207
00:17:00.280 --> 00:17:08.580
truthful and fair to the parties, to our country, and to our people to allow those abroad,

208
00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:12.020
looking at the pyramids along denial,

209
00:17:12.020 --> 00:17:16.100
or shopping in the fashion houses of Paris,

210
00:17:16.100 --> 00:17:19.380
or riding the romantic gondolas of Venice,

211
00:17:19.380 --> 00:17:23.300
or deliberately hiding in the dark corners of the world,

212
00:17:23.300 --> 00:17:29.300
while everyone here, everyone here in this hall,

213
00:17:29.300 --> 00:17:33.860
is sweating it out, listening to sometimes irrelevant

214
00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:38.260
and loquacious lawyers, or to humble an ancient

215
00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:41.180
amicus curate like me.

216
00:17:42.300 --> 00:17:44.220
To include your honors,

217
00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:49.780
may I say that you are tasked with a constitutional duty

218
00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:55.900
that cannot always be reduced to abstract arithmetic.

219
00:17:56.820 --> 00:18:01.820
Neither can such duty be performed in the shadows of absence,

220
00:18:04.940 --> 00:18:07.860
nor from legal impediments.

221
00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:11.820
as the elected representatives of the Filipino people,

222
00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:15.100
your honor's mandate, in my humble opinion,

223
00:18:15.100 --> 00:18:20.100
demands a common sensical, common sensical, I repeat,

224
00:18:21.900 --> 00:18:25.660
common sensical interpretation of the Constitution.

225
00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:30.220
Indeed, meaningful adjudication requires

226
00:18:30.220 --> 00:18:35.220
active participation in the search for truth and fairness.

227
00:18:35.220 --> 00:18:43.540
I respectfully submit that only in this manner can your honors ensure a verdict that is fair

228
00:18:43.540 --> 00:18:52.020
to the parties, fair to your honors peers, and ultimately fair to our sovereign people.

229
00:18:52.020 --> 00:19:02.000
Maraming salamat po muli sa inyong pa anyaya at masusing pa kikining sa inyong abang lingkot. Maraming salamat po.

230
00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:19.000
Maraming salamat din po CJ Panganiban, tohos po subod namin pinaparating sa inyo. Ang pasasalamat hindi lamang ng hukuman ito pero ng sambayanan sa oras at karunungan at karanasangin nilahad din yos amin. So maging ito. Thank you sir.
